config BR2_PACKAGE_FLIPPER_BTRFS_TOOLS
	bool "flipper-btrfs-tools"
	help
	  Flipper btrfs profile/snapshot tooling: create/delete/rename
	  profiles, snapshot send/receive/delete, maintenance, and
	  show-space. Their -d mode targets the unmounted profiles
	  partition, so they run from recovery against the internal
	  btrfs. Installed to /usr/local/sbin, with every shared helper
	  the tools source (flipper-btrfs.sh, flipper-bls.sh,
	  flipper-rootinfo.sh and the account-merge awk script) in
	  /usr/lib.

	  Runtime deps (enabled separately in the defconfig): btrfs-progs,
	  compsize, duperemove, git (migrate-profile's `git merge-file` merge
	  engine), diffutils (its `cmp`), acl (its `rsync -aHAX` needs ACL
	  support), findmnt/flock (util-linux), mawk. migrate-profile replays
	  packages with the profile's own apt inside a chroot, so recovery
	  itself needs no apt/dpkg.

	  https://github.com/flipperdevices/flipperos-btrfs-tools
